<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 2.2 PCT IN OCTOBER - NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 2.2 PCT IN OCTOBER - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 2.74</p>
<p>billion zlotys, or 2.2 percent, in October to 126.04 billion</p>
<p>after a 1.2 percent rise in September, preliminary central bank</p>
<p>figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 20.9 percent in the January-October</p>
<p>period against 26.1 percent in the same period of last year.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		   OCTOBER   SEPT	   OCT 95</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	     2.2    1.2		3.0</p>
<p>  Money (in bln PLN)		   126.04 123.30(123.23)  97.45</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)     22.51  22.39	    20.84</p>
<p>  National currency (in bln PLN)   103.53 100.91(100.84)  76.61</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation (in bln PLN)  23.51  23.02	    18.52</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector   73.41  70.62(70.57)   53.48</p>
<p>(in bln PLN)</p>
<p>NOTE: revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
